<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa clothing industry, union agree wage deal.</title>
<headline>S.Africa clothing industry, union agree wage deal.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's clothing industry, which was hit by a national strike over pay last year, has reached a wages deal for the year to June 1998, the Cape Clothing Manufacturers' Association said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The industry said in a statement that it had agreed on pay, bonuses, leave and healthcare beenfits with the South African Clothing and Textile Workers' Union.</p>
<p>The agreement includes a nine percent wage increase across the board and a one percent increase to provident fund contributions by employers from January 1, 1998.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
